  "slug": "contact-domain-dd02",
  "summary": "Protein language models are now being fused with structural and interface information across antibody, complex, pocket, and enzyme prediction tasks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is pretrained protein language model representations (ESM-2, ESM3, ESM-IF) coupled to structural or interface information to score candidate complexes, pockets and residues. AbAffinity uses frozen ESM-2 embeddings for sequence-only antibody-antigen affinity, and ParaEM predicts paratope residues from sequence with ESM3 embeddings and antigen-aware scoring. Candidate selection is a second theme: DeepUMQA-Selection pairs accuracy estimators with USR-based alignment, and EnsPlex merges docking and AlphaFold-family models under a DockQ-supervised scorer. New elements include training-free pocket exploration in ACER and preference optimization of a frozen ESM-IF decoder in SimBinder-IF, with modest reported gains. Generative design and conformal uncertainty papers are adjacent rather than part of this scaffold, and a leakage analysis of enzyme-substrate prediction shows similarity-driven inflation of reported performance.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-05"
}
